`evaluateFieldVisibility` returns immediately after evaluating `visibleOn`, so if a field specifies both `visibleOn` and `dependsOn`, the `dependsOn` constraint is ignored. Consider combining them (e.g., require both to be true) so multiple visibility conditions compose predictably.
```suggestion
  let isVisible = true;

  // Evaluate visibleOn expression
  if (fieldConfig.visibleOn) {
    try {
      const evaluator = new ExpressionEvaluator({
        data: formValues,
        form: formValues,
      });
      isVisible = evaluator.evaluateCondition(fieldConfig.visibleOn);
    } catch {
      // On error, default to visible
      isVisible = true;
    }
  }

  if (!isVisible) {
    return false;
  }

  // Evaluate dependsOn: field is hidden if parent field has no value
  if (fieldConfig.dependsOn) {
    const parentValue = formValues[fieldConfig.dependsOn];
    const hasParentValue =
      parentValue !== undefined && parentValue !== null && parentValue !== '';
    if (!hasParentValue) {
